gamescope: ignore Steam's frame-rate-cap control so our cap sticks

The KONKR gamescope session owns its frame-rate cap (konkr-session-client on
session start, device-controls live -- both via debug_set_fps_limit). With no
QAM Performance tab, Steam pushes its own value through gamescope_control on
connect (the panel refresh = effectively uncapped), which reset the app
refresh-cycle override and clobbered our cap every session. Make the control a
no-op; our cap is authoritative.

--- a/src/wlserver.cpp
+++ b/src/wlserver.cpp
@@ -1098,15 +1098,12 @@
 
 static void gamescope_control_set_app_target_refresh_cycle( struct wl_client *client, struct wl_resource *resource, uint32_t fps, uint32_t flags )
 {
-	auto display_type = gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_EXTERNAL;
-	if ( flags & GAMESCOPE_CONTROL_TARGET_REFRESH_CYCLE_FLAG_INTERNAL_DISPLAY )
-		display_type = gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_INTERNAL;
-
-	steamcompmgr_set_app_refresh_cycle_override(
-		display_type,
-		fps,
-		!!( flags & GAMESCOPE_CONTROL_TARGET_REFRESH_CYCLE_FLAG_ALLOW_REFRESH_SWITCHING ),
-		!( flags & GAMESCOPE_CONTROL_TARGET_REFRESH_CYCLE_FLAG_ONLY_CHANGE_REFRESH_RATE ) );
+	// KONKR: fully ignore Steam's frame-rate-cap control. The cap is owned by us
+	// (konkr-session-client on session start + device-controls live, both via
+	// debug_set_fps_limit). With no QAM Performance tab, Steam pushes its own
+	// value through this control on connect -- the panel refresh, i.e. effectively
+	// uncapped -- which clobbered our cap back every session. Do nothing.
+	(void)client; (void)resource; (void)fps; (void)flags;
 }
 
 static void gamescope_control_take_screenshot( struct wl_client *client, struct wl_resource *resource, const char *path, uint32_t type, uint32_t flags )
